# Every text file is stored with LF line endings, in the working tree too. The release build
# packs payload files exactly as they sit in the tree, and the shipped artifacts must be
# byte-identical no matter which platform builds them (docs/RELEASE.md): a Windows checkout
# must not turn the payload into CRLF. The LF scripts are what setup runs on Windows
# PowerShell 5.1, which reads LF text correctly.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.ico binary
